### Archive Browsing

KKC can browse ZIP archives as if they were directories.
Press ENTER on a supported archive file to enter it.

Supported formats: ZIP, LHA/LZH, Amstrad CPC disk images, Commodore D64 disk images.

Inside an archive you can:
- Navigate the directory tree
- View files with the internal viewer (F3)
- Copy files out of the archive to a normal directory (F5)

Creating or modifying archives is not supported from within the browser.

### Remote Browsing (SFTP / IMAP)

KKC supports remote file systems via SFTP and IMAP.

#### Connect to Remote Host

Press Ctrl-F to open the connection panel.

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| UP/DOWN | browse saved profiles |
| Type | filter profiles by name |
| ENTER | connect to selected profile |
| F6 | edit selected profile |
| F7 | add new SFTP profile |
| F8 | add new IMAP profile |
| ESC | close panel |

#### SFTP fields

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Name | profile display name |
| Host | hostname or IP address |
| Port | SSH port (default 22) |
| User | login username |
| Password | login password (stored in profile file) |
| Remote dir | initial directory after connect |

#### IMAP fields

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Name | profile display name |
| Host | IMAP server hostname |
| Port | IMAP port (default 993) |
| User | email address / username |
| Password | password |

#### Navigation in Remote Panel

Navigation works the same as locally.
   File operations (view, copy out, delete, rename) are supported.
   Editing uploads the file back after the editor exits.

## Commands in Details

### View File (Internal Viewer)

#### Opening

F3 on any file opens the internal viewer.
The viewer automatically detects the file type:

| Type | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Text | plain text or source code |
| Hex | binary or unknown format |
| Ansi | file containing ANSI escape sequences |
| Image | PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WebP |

#### Navigation

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| UP / DOWN | Scroll one line up / down. |
| PGUP / PGDN | Scroll one page up / down. |
| HOME | Go to beginning of file. |
| END | Go to end of file. |
| LEFT / RIGHT | Scroll 8 columns left / right (Text mode). |
| C-LEFT / C-RIGHT | Scroll 40 columns left / right. |
| C-HOME | Scroll to column 0. |
| g | Open goto dropdown. |

| Goto key | Description |
| --- | --- |
| g | Go to line number <n>, or file start if no <n>. |
| e | Go to last line. |
| s | Go to first non-blank line. |
| n | Go to next page. |
| p | Go to previous page. |

#### Search

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| F7 or / | Open search bar. |
| n | Jump to next match. |
| N | Jump to previous match. |
| C-N | Jump to next match (alternative). |
| C-J / C-K | Open next / previous file from the active panel. |

#### Viewer menus (F-keys)

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| F2 | Toggle word wrap (Text / Ansi modes). |
| F3 | Line-feed mode: DOS (CR/LF) \| Unix (LF) \| Mac (CR) \| Mixed. |
| F4 | View mode: Text \| Binary (Hex) \| Ansi \| Image \| Plugin viewer. |
| F5 | Toggle zoom (fullscreen / windowed). |
| F6 | Pre-processing pipeline (XOR, AND, OR, NEG, ROR, ADD, Latin, Elite). |
| F8 | Encoding: Plain ASCII \| DOS CP437. |
| F9 | [Keyword mask](#mask-configuration) style: C \| Pascal \| Assembler \| Ketchup \| Off. |

#### Closing

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| ESC or F10 | Return to file panel. |

### Search Files

Open: Alt-F7 or Tools > Search

The search panel has two input fields:

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Filename | glob pattern (e.g. *.log, report*) |
| Content | optional text to search inside files |

Press TAB to switch between the two fields. Press ENTER to start the search.
Results appear below; UP/DOWN to navigate them. Press ENTER on a result to jump to that file's directory. Press ESC to close the panel.

### Edit File

F4 on any local file launches the editor configured in Options > Setup.
The default editor is taken from the EDITOR environment variable or from the 'editor' setting in the config file.

If the editor field is empty (editor = ""), F4 opens the selected local file in the [Internal editor](#internal-editor) side panel instead.

For remote files the file is downloaded, edited locally, then uploaded back automatically when the external editor exits.

When config.toml is modified and saved, KKC reloads the configuration.

### Internal Editor

The internal editor is shown inside a side panel and is used by F4 when Options > Setup > Editor is empty (editor = "").

#### Keys

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| C-S | Save file. |
| A-Z | Toggle word wrap. Wrap is off by default. |
| TAB | Leave editor focus and return to the opposite panel. |
| ESC | Close editor; asks before discarding unsaved changes. |

With wrap off, long lines scroll horizontally to keep the cursor visible. With wrap on, long lines are wrapped to the panel width.

Saving config.toml from the internal editor reloads the configuration immediately.

### Copy File

F5 copies the selected files (or the current file if nothing is selected) to the other panel's directory.

Copy dialog fields:

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Destination | target path (editable) |
| Overwrite | overwrite existing files |
| Newer only | only copy if source is newer |
| Keep attributes | preserve timestamps and permissions |

Navigation: Tab / Up / Down between fields. Space toggles checkboxes. Enter or OK starts the copy. ESC cancels.

### Move File

F6 moves selected files to the other panel's directory. Same dialog as [Copy](#copy-file).

### Create Directory

F7 opens a name prompt. Type the new directory name and press Enter. ESC cancels.

### Delete Files

F8 deletes the selected files (or current file). A confirmation dialog is shown if 'Confirm delete' is enabled in [Options > Setup](#configuration).

### Rename File

Shift-F6 opens a rename prompt pre-filled with the current filename. Edit and press Enter to rename. ESC cancels.

### Select Files by Pattern

The '+' key opens a wildcard dialog. Default pattern is '*'. Examples: `*.txt`, `report_??.* `

### Deselect Files by Pattern

The '-' key opens a wildcard dialog to deselect matching files.

### Invert Selection

The '*' key inverts the current selection (selected becomes unselected and vice versa).

### Directory Bookmarks

Ctrl-D opens the bookmarks panel, which shows saved directory paths.

- Type to filter bookmarks by name
- UP / DOWN to navigate the list
- ENTER to jump to the selected directory
- DELETE to remove the selected bookmark
- The first item is always "Add current directory"
- Backspace deletes the last filter character
- ESC closes the panel

### Installation

KKC is available on:
- **Homebrew (macOS/Linux):** 
```sh
brew install redbug26/tap/kkc
```
- **Build from source:** 
```sh
git clone https://github.com/redbug26/kkc-rust.git
cd kkc-rust
cargo build --release
```

Requirements: Rust stable toolchain. On Linux: also libssl-dev.

### Bundled Plugins

KKC ships with pre-installed plugins:

| Plugin | Format Support |
| --- | --- |
| text_syntax | Rust, C/C++, Lua, JS/TS syntax highlighting |
| csv_viewer | CSV table viewing with word-wrap |
| json_viewer | Formatted JSON viewer |
| markdown_viewer | Rendered Markdown viewer |
| html_viewer | HTML viewer |
| eml_viewer | Email (.eml) files |
| pdf_file | PDF viewer |
| lha_lzh | LHA/LZH archive support |
| amstrad_dsk | Amstrad CPC disk image browser |
| commodore_d64 | Commodore 64 disk image browser |

Press Enter on a `.kkplug` file to install custom plugins.

### Custom Lua Plugins

KKC supports Lua plugins that extend the viewer and file handling.

Each plugin is a directory (or .kkplug bundle) containing:

| File | Description |
| --- | --- |
| plugin.lua | Lua script |
| plugin.toml | metadata (name, version, description) |

Installed plugins are stored in the user data directory. Press Enter on a .kkplug file to install it automatically.

Options > Plugins opens the plugin list:

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| UP / DOWN | navigate |
| ENTER / O | open plugin directory |
| ESC / F10 | close |

Plugins can provide custom viewers that appear in the F4 viewer mode picker as "Plugins viewer > [plugin name]".

### File Associations

Options > Associations manages per-extension openers.

For each extension you can define one or more commands. Use '%f' as a placeholder for the file path, or the path is appended automatically.

   Example:

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Extension | mp4 |
| Openers | mpv %f, vlc %f |

If multiple openers exist for a file, a picker is shown on ENTER.

   Association editor keys:

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| A / + / F1 | Add new association |
| ENTER / E | Edit selected |
| DELETE / D | Delete selected |
| ESC | Close |

## Lua Applications

KKC can run Lua applications (games, tools, utilities) inside the terminal.

Use **Tools > Run Lua app** to browse and launch installed applications.

Applications can access:
- File system operations
- Graphics rendering (text-based)
- Keyboard and mouse input
- KKC internals via `kkc` module

For developers, see the template in `assets/applications/template_lua_app`.

## Menu System

### Menu Bar

F2 (or the F2 button in the key bar) opens the menu bar.

| Menu | Entries |
| --- | --- |
| File | View, Edit, Copy, Move, Mkdir, Rename, Delete, Quit |
| Panel | Swap panels, Sort, Toggle hidden, Reload |
| Disk | Go to path |
| Selection | Select, Deselect, Invert |
| Tools | Search, Bookmarks |
| Options | Setup, Plugins, Associations, F-Key bar, Save Config |
| Help | Help, About |

Navigation: LEFT / RIGHT between menus (wraps around). UP / DOWN within a menu. ENTER or first-letter shortcut to activate. ESC closes the menu.

### Keyword Mask (Viewer)

In Text or Ansi viewer mode, F9 opens the mask menu:

| Style | Description |
| --- | --- |
| C Style | highlights C/C++ keywords |
| Pascal Style | highlights Pascal keywords |
| Assembler Style | highlights x86 assembler mnemonics |
| Ketchup Style | highlights a custom keyword set |
| Mask OFF | disable highlighting |

The mask is rendered as bold text on the current line.

### Configuration (Options > Setup)

Setup is split into tabs. Use LEFT / RIGHT, PAGEUP / PAGEDOWN, ALT-LEFT / ALT-RIGHT or CTRL-LEFT / CTRL-RIGHT to switch tab. Use UP / DOWN or TAB / SHIFT-TAB to move inside the active tab.

#### Checkboxes

| Option | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Confirm exit | Ask before quitting KKC. |
| Confirm delete | Ask before deleting files. |
| Auto reload | Reload panel after file operations. |
| Insert moves down | Cursor moves down after pressing Insert. |
| Select directories | Include directories in wildcard selection. |
| Show hidden files | Display hidden / dot files. |
| Color by type | Color entries by file type / extension. |
| Cloud icons | Show a cloud icon for files available only online. |
| File icons | Show folder and file-type icons in panels. |
| Show F-key bar | Display the function-key shortcut bar. |

#### Text Fields

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Editor | Command to launch for F4 (e.g. nano, vim, code). |
| Pager | Command for viewing large text files. |
| Dir history max | Maximum number of entries in directory bookmarks. |

Leave empty to use the internal editor for local files.

#### Buttons

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| OK / Enter | Apply and save configuration. |
| Cancel / ESC | Discard changes. |

### Help

F1 (or the Help menu item) displays this help documentation.

In the help viewer:
- **Navigation:** UP / DOWN to scroll, PGUP / PGDN to page
- **Tabs:** Press TAB to navigate between links in the text
- **Search:** F7 or / to search for text
- **Sections:** Click on or navigate to underlined links to jump to sections
- **Close:** Press ESC or F10 to return to the file manager

### Quit

F10 exits KKC. A confirmation dialog appears if:
- "Confirm exit" is enabled in [Options > Setup](#configuration-options--setup)
- There are unsaved changes in the internal editor
- There are ongoing operations

## About

### About KKC

KKC - **Ketchup Killers Commander**

Rust rewrite by [RedBug](#contact) (Miguel Vanhove)

Originally created in 1997 as a DOS file manager. This version is a complete rewrite in Rust using the ratatui TUI library.

**Source code and releases:** https://github.com/redbug26/kkc-rust

**Report bugs and ideas:** GitHub Issues

### Contact

- **GitHub:** https://github.com/redbug26
- **Issues:** https://github.com/redbug26/kkc-rust/issues

### History

**Version 0.1.18**
- Error/status messages now displayed in a proper dialog box
- Tab support: multiple tabs per panel, tabs saved and restored across sessions
- Viewer optimisation: faster rendering, viewer split into sub-modules
- CSV viewer: word-wrap support for long cells
- XML viewer plugin added
- MIME type detection used throughout
- IDF/file-ID probing extended: many more formats recognised
- Amstrad CPC & C64 Disk plugin: improved directory listing
- Viewer highlight submenu: new sub-menu to control syntax/keyword highlighting
- Panels refactored
- FileID panel improvement

**Version 0.1.17**
- Complete rewrite in Rust using ratatui + crossterm
- Dual-panel TUI with tab support in each panel
- Internal viewer: Text / Hex / Ansi / Image modes (lazy decoding)
- Archive browsing (ZIP)
- Remote browsing: SFTP and IMAP
- Lua plugin system with viewer plugins
- File associations with multi-opener picker
- Directory bookmarks with fuzzy filter
- File search by name and content
- macOS/linux Homebrew distribution

**Original DOS Version (1997)**

KKC was originally created as a DOS file manager in 1997, featuring dual-panel navigation, archive support, and extensive file operations. The Rust version (2026) is a complete rewrite maintaining the same workflow philosophy while leveraging modern TUI capabilities.
